      "summary": "A process analog. Gobustan holds one of the world's largest concentrations of mud volcanoes. On Mars, mud volcanism is a leading explanation for thousands of mounds in Arabia Terra and Chryse/Acidalia, linked to subsurface fluids, methane and possible biosignatures. Its value is as a natural laboratory for interpreting Martian mounds, testing methane and fluid-sampling instruments, and training rovers on soft mud breccia.",
      "facts": [
        "Surface up to ≈ 318 K (+45 °C)",
        "Down to ≈ 269 K (−4 °C)",
        "NDVI ≈ 0.15",
        "Day–night swing ≈ 14 K"
      ],
      "breaks": "It gets far more rain than the Atacama. Its volcanoes are driven by hydrocarbons, under a thick atmosphere and full Earth gravity."
